{
  "name": "02-failed-review-rework",
  "description": "A review fails and the previous builder, who holds nothing, gets a fresh lease, acknowledges again, reworks and resubmits; the second review passes. At the first submit only one provider is connected, so No reviewer is eligible opens, and it closes when the owner connects a reviewer of another provider.",
  "covers": [
    "PRD Rework and escalation: a failed review adds one to the round, reopens the failed criterion and gives the free previous builder a fresh lease (review.failed carries lease_seat_id, plan SM-7).",
    "PRD Steps and timing, the step table sentence: review.failed opens wait_builder, task.briefing_acknowledged closes it and opens rework, task.submitted closes rework.",
    "Plan SM-42: No reviewer is eligible opens beside task.submitted while only the builder's provider has a reviewer, and resolves in the connect_seat command that adds a reviewer of another provider.",
    "PRD Shipped rules: Repeated failed reviews move a task to a stronger model writes no rule check row after one failure, because it does not change the outcome (How a transition is gated, step 7)."
  ],
